# Bottom Navigation Layout Rules

Locked files: `src/components/BottomNav.tsx`, rendered once as a **direct child of `<body>`** in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Do not add a second nav in pages. Do not wrap it in `<main>`, flex shells, or page layouts.

- The outer `<nav>` stays `fixed bottom-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 h-[64px] w-full bg-background border-t border-border/30`.
- Do NOT add `pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)]`, `pb-safe`, or `mb-safe` on the nav. Home-indicator clearance is a fixed inner `pb-3` only.
- Inner wrapper MUST remain `flex h-full w-full items-center justify-around px-2 pb-3` so icons and labels sit above the home indicator.
- Do NOT modify or recalculate this component when editing page-level layouts.

Page scroll clearance stays on `main.app-scroll` as `pb-[72px]`. That is not nav padding; do not move it onto the `<nav>`.
